## Copy rules
- Allowed claims, each with its source:
  - "<claim>" — <site / store / app string>
- Forbidden for this app (from the listings, your memory notes, or the user):
  - e.g. never "no ads" if the Play listing says "Contains ads"
  - e.g. no ratings, reviews, download counts, % or money figures
- AI features are framed as help, never as guaranteed.
- The app name is always written as: <exact spelling>
- AI-generated label text in this language: <e.g. "AI-generated">

## Music
- Source: ACE-Step 1.5 / MusicGen / the user's own track (copy its bgm_user.source.txt here).
- Prompt, chosen seed, tempo (--bpm), drop bar, synthetic lift yes/no (music_rank.py table).
- The licence note of that source was shown to the user.

## Reference
Optional. Fill it only when the user gives a reference video or image for the look. Delete the
section when there is none. A reference is for the craft, never for the content.
- Reference: <file or link the user gave> (what it is, who made it)
- Palette: a colour per role, sampled with `sample_colors.py <image> <points.json>` on a frame of the
  reference (points.json maps a name to `[x, y]` in 0..1). Write a value you judged by eye as "estimated".
- Typography: weight, case, size against the frame, how tight the lines are.
- Composition: where the subject sits, how much empty space, what is cropped.
- Pacing: how many seconds between changes, and where the changes land.
- Motion: which motion class each move belongs to (`references/motion.md`).
- Texture: grain, glow, shadow, blur, or none.
- Do not copy: the logo, the characters, the text, the music, any claim and any product screen of the reference.

## What NOT to do
- No invented stats, ratings, people, testimonials or quotes.
- No linear full-screen gradients (banding): radial only.
- No pasted raw screenshots: rebuild the UI as HTML.
- Never remove the AI-generated label.
